#: source/glossary.md:387
msgid "\\[string interpolation\\]{#gloss-string-interpolation}"
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:389
msgid ""
"Expanding expressions enclosed in `${ }` within a [string](./language/types."
"md#type-string), [path](./language/types.md#type-path), or [attribute name]"
"(./language/types.md#type-attrs)."
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:391
msgid ""
"See [String interpolation](./language/string-interpolation.md) for details."
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:397
msgid "[SRI](#gloss-sri){#gloss-sri}"
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:399
msgid ""
"[Subresource Integrity](https://www.w3.org/TR/SRI/) (SRI) is a [W3C "
"specification](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/"
"Subresource_Integrity) for integrity metadata. Nix uses the SRI hash format "
"(`<algorithm>-<Base64 hash>`) to specify content hashes in a way that is "
"self-describing, since the hash algorithm is part of the format."
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:404
msgid "\\[substitute\\]{#gloss-substitute}"
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:406
msgid ""
"A substitute is a command invocation stored in the [Nix database](#gloss-nix-"
"database) that describes how to build a store object, bypassing the normal "
"build mechanism (i.e., derivations). Typically, the substitute builds the "
"store object by downloading a pre-built version of the store object from "
"some server."
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:412
msgid "[substituter](#gloss-substituter){#gloss-substituter}"
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:414
msgid ""
"An additional [store](#gloss-store){#gloss-store} from which Nix can obtain "
"store objects instead of building them. Often the substituter is a [binary "
"cache](#gloss-binary-cache), but any store can serve as substituter."
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:417
msgid ""
"See the [`substituters` configuration option](./command-ref/conf-file."
"md#conf-substituters) for details."
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:421
msgid "\\[user environment\\]{#gloss-user-env}"
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:423
msgid ""
"An automatically generated store object that consists of a set of symlinks "
"to “active” applications, i.e., other store paths. These are generated "
"automatically by [`nix-env`](./command-ref/nix-env.md). See _profiles_."
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:428
msgid "[validity](#gloss-validity){#gloss-validity}"
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:430
msgid ""
"A store path is valid if all [store object](#gloss-store-object)s in its "
"[closure](#gloss-closure) can be read from the [store](#gloss-store)."
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:432
msgid "For a [local store](./store/types/local-store.md), this means:"
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:433
msgid ""
"The store path leads to an existing [store object](#gloss-store-object) in "
"that [store](#gloss-store)."
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:434
msgid ""
"The store path is listed in the [Nix database](#gloss-nix-database) as being "
"valid."
msgstr ""

#: source/glossary.md:435
msgid "All paths in the store path's [closure](#gloss-closure) are valid."
msgstr ""
